  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1102 PM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nTemperatures will trend warmer through mid-week as 500mb blow\nbecomes more zonal and the surface ridge moves east, placing us\nin southerly flow between the ridge an a developing low over the\nSW CONUS. Look for highs in the mid 40s to mid 50s Monday,\nincreasing to the 60s Wednesday and Thursday. Friday looks to be\ncooler following the potential passage of a system.\n\nPrecip chances around 60% return Thursday and Friday as \nensembles show an upper low and surface low moving from the SW \nCONUS to the central CONUS. Thunderstorms will be possible given\nthe warm airmass in place and potential strength of the system.",
